From d450b2a9e13ca4fa2b6a59f5cf1f0250f6423e31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:38:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/43] GS: software rasterizer for render targets the game
 reads back

Targets a game downloads (directly, or after copying them elsewhere) are drawn by CGsSwRaster straight
into GS memory, following the GS rules: top-left fill, 4 bit bilinear weights, mip level from Q/L/K,
integer blending and tests, destination formats. ATV Offroad Fury 2 computes its near terrain on the
GS (VIF codes as flat sprites, noise textures blended per mip level, heights from interpolated Z) and
downloads the result as VIF packets: the GL renderer can't give those bits back.
